<title>JAPAN: Toyota says output resumes at all domestic plants.</title>
<headline>Toyota says output resumes at all domestic plants.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production at all of Toyota Motor Corp's domestic plants resumed on Friday, a Toyota spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>A fire last Saturday at a plant of Aisin Seiki Co Ltd prevented output of brake parts supplied to Toyota, forcing the idling of all the carmaker's domestic plants on Tuesday, except for those of Daihatsu Motor Co Ltd, and halting 22 out of a total of 30 production lines on Monday.</p>
</text>
